{
  "_NOTE": "Email bridge via IMAP (inbound) + SMTP (outbound). Use an app-specific password for Gmail / iCloud / Outlook etc. Whitelist contains sender email addresses (lowercase). Setup walkthrough: README -> Email bridge.",
  "_NOTE_chat_profiles": "Default is MAXIMUM OPEN (--dangerously-skip-permissions, all tools). To RESTRICT bot behaviour for individual senders, add a 'chat_profiles' object keyed by the sender email. Hot-reload applies immediately.",
  "imap_host": "imap.gmail.com",
  "imap_port": 993,
  "imap_secure": true,
  "imap_user": "you@example.com",
  "imap_password": "YOUR_IMAP_APP_PASSWORD",
  "imap_mailbox": "INBOX",
  "imap_poll_seconds": 30,
  "smtp_host": "smtp.gmail.com",
  "smtp_port": 465,
  "smtp_secure": true,
  "smtp_user": "you@example.com",
  "smtp_password": "YOUR_SMTP_APP_PASSWORD",
  "from_address": "you@example.com",
  "from_name": "Claude Bridge",
  "subject_prefix": "[Claude] ",
  "whitelist": [],
  "rate_limit_per_hour": 30,
  "pin": null,
  "_NOTE_security": "Inbound email is authenticated by DMARC/DKIM alignment (the From header alone is forgeable). A message is only trusted when the receiving provider's top Authentication-Results line shows dmarc=pass (or aligned dkim=pass) AND that line's authserv-id is provably the receiver's. The expected authserv-id is DERIVED FROM imap_host (2026-09-07): reading imap.gmail.com trusts only Google's ids, outlook.office365.com only Microsoft's, and so on for iCloud/Yahoo. Any other imap_host (self-hosted, or a gateway such as Mimecast/Proofpoint in front of your mailbox) has NO auto-recognised receiver and you MUST set auth_results_authserv_id to your provider's authserv-id — otherwise every message is dropped, and before this change an attacker could simply inject 'Authentication-Results: mx.google.com; dmarc=pass' and be trusted. RFC 5322 comments and quoted strings in the Authentication-Results line are stripped before parsing, so a d=/i= value hidden in a comment cannot forge alignment. An empty whitelist DENIES all senders (use the PIN /auth flow to claim owner). Set dev_mode:true ONLY for local testing to restore legacy open behaviour.",
  "dev_mode": false,
  "auth_results_authserv_id": null
}
